# Tech Stack
- Next.js 14 (App Router)
- React 18
- Tailwind CSS 3
- Lucide React (for icons)
- JavaScript (JSX)

# Project Context
This is a landing page and informational website for "Period Tracker & Ovulation Cycle", a mobile application focused on reproductive health, AI cycle reports, Ayurveda care, and privacy. 

# Coding Conventions & Styling Guidelines
- **Architecture**: App Router (`src/app`). All pages are `.jsx` and use standard Next.js routing.
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS exclusively.
- **Typography Standards**:
  - Do NOT manually size headings (e.g., `text-4xl`, `sm:text-5xl`). Headings (`h1`, `h2`, `h3`, `h4`, `h5`, `h6`) are globally defined in `src/app/globals.css` under `@layer base`.
  - Paragraphs (`<p>`) strictly default to 16px (`1rem`). Do NOT add custom size classes (like `text-sm` or `text-lg`) to `<p>` tags.
  - For small descriptive text (14px) inside cards or FAQs, use `<div className="text-sm">` rather than a `<p>` tag.
- **Components**: UI components are located in `src/components`. Keep them modular and reusable.
- **State Management**: React Hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useMemo`).
- **Icons**: Use `lucide-react` for all iconography.

# Do's and Don'ts
- **DO**: Maintain the strict global typography rules. Use Tailwind for all styling.
- **DO**: Ensure mobile responsiveness using Tailwind's `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` prefixes where necessary (except for headings/p tags which are globally handled).
- **DON'T**: Use absolute text sizes for standard structural text overriding the global theme.
- **DON'T**: Create fake legal representatives or falsify legal information in the Privacy Policy.
- **DON'T**: Expose sensitive API endpoints or tokens.
